    "reasoning": "To handle 1M PDFs daily, Amazon S3 is used for secure file storage with server-side encryption. AWS Lambda processes documents in a serverless manner, allowing for automatic scaling based on the workload. Amazon ECS is utilized for containerized applications that perform heavier processing tasks. By using Amazon API Gateway, the architecture ensures secure access to the processing services while maintaining scalability. This setup balances cost, as AWS Lambda charges only for the compute time consumed, making it cost-effective for sporadic workloads.\n\nThe system employs Amazon RDS for transactional data storage, ensuring ACID compliance for any metadata or user information related to documents processed. In addition, Amazon DynamoDB provides a NoSQL solution for high-velocity access patterns, ensuring performance and reliability. Amazon SQS facilitates decoupling of components, allowing the architecture to handle bursts in document submissions without losing messages. Overall, this architecture is designed to be resilient and cost-effective, scaling with demand while ensuring data is encrypted both at rest and in transit."
