    "reasoning": "To achieve scalability, we leverage AWS Lambda for serverless compute which can automatically scale based on demand while Amazon ECS can manage containerized applications for more complex workloads. The use of Amazon API Gateway enables us to create and manage secure APIs effectively, allowing for efficient request routing and throttling. For data storage, Amazon RDS can provide relational database services for structured data with per-customer isolation through separate schemas or databases, while Amazon DynamoDB is ideal for unstructured data with high availability and performance. Amazon CloudFront serves as a content delivery network to reduce latency and improve user experience by caching static assets close to users.\n\nFor reliability, data is stored in multiple Availability Zones (AZs) with Amazon RDS, ensuring high availability and durability. AWS Lambda and Amazon ECS allow us to handle variable workloads without over-provisioning resources, thus optimizing costs. Overall, this architecture provides a balance between cost-effectiveness and performance, as the serverless components minimize idle resource costs while still providing a robust infrastructure to handle varying loads."
