    "reasoning": "AWS IoT Core is essential for securely connecting and managing a large number of IoT devices. It provides a reliable way to ingest data from the devices with support for MQTT and HTTP protocols. For processing real-time data, Amazon Kinesis Data Streams allows for event-driven architecture, enabling data to be processed immediately as it's received. AWS Lambda is then used to process that data in a serverless manner, allowing for automatic scaling based on incoming data volume, which is crucial for handling spikes in traffic from 100,000 devices.\n\nFor data storage, Amazon DynamoDB is chosen for its ability to handle high-velocity data with low-latency access patterns. It provides a fully managed NoSQL database solution that scales automatically and is cost-effective for variable workloads. Amazon SNS and SQS are included for messaging purposes, facilitating communication between different components of the architecture. Monitoring is accomplished using Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray to ensure that all components are functioning correctly and to provide insights into performance and bottlenecks.",
