    "reasoning": "The architecture leverages AWS Lambda for serverless processing, allowing for on-demand execution of code to transform and load data without the need for provisioning and managing servers. Amazon RDS serves as the primary transactional database, while Amazon Redshift is optimized for analytical queries, making it suitable for the client's data warehousing needs. Using AWS DMS simplifies the CDC process by automatically capturing changes in the RDS database and replicating them to Redshift, ensuring data consistency and minimizing latency. Kinesis Data Streams can be used for real-time data ingestion, providing a scalable solution for high-throughput data capture. This architecture is designed to be cost-effective, as it minimizes idle resources and only incurs costs when processing data.",
