      "reason": "AWS Lambda provides a fully managed, serverless compute environment that scales automatically based on demand, which is ideal for the event-driven architecture of the saga pattern. It also reduces costs as you only pay for the execution time.",
      "when_to_switch": "If the application requires long-running processes or specific custom runtime environments that Lambda cannot support, then EC2 might be a better choice."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Amazon EventBridge vs. SNS/SQS",
      "chose": "Amazon EventBridge",
      "reason": "EventBridge provides a more sophisticated event routing mechanism that allows for better integration with other AWS services and supports complex event patterns, which is beneficial for orchestrating the saga pattern across multiple microservices.",
      "when_to_switch": "If the use case requires simple message queuing without the need for complex event routing, then using SNS or SQS may suffice."
