      ],
      "messaging": [
        "Amazon SQS (if needed for decoupling)"
      ],
      "monitoring": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch"
      ]
    },
    "reasoning": "AWS Lambda is chosen for compute as it allows for serverless execution of code in response to scheduled events, making it cost-effective and scalable. By using Amazon EventBridge (formerly CloudWatch Events), we can easily trigger the Lambda function at a specified time each night, ensuring that the report generation is automated and reliable. This architecture eliminates the need for managing servers, reducing operational overhead and costs. For data storage, Amazon RDS or DynamoDB can be used depending on the structure and size of the data; RDS is ideal for relational data while DynamoDB is suited for NoSQL data, providing flexibility based on the client's needs.

Using Amazon API Gateway allows for easy integration and management of any APIs that may be needed for report generation or retrieval. CloudFront can be used as a CDN to cache and deliver reports efficiently. Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch will provide insights into the performance and execution of the Lambda functions, allowing for proactive management and troubleshooting."
