    "reasoning": "The architecture utilizes Amazon CloudFront as a CDN to cache content at the edge, significantly reducing latency and offloading traffic from the origin. The AWS Application Load Balancer will distribute incoming requests across multiple compute resources, ensuring high availability and scalability. AWS Lambda is chosen for its serverless compute capability to handle variable loads, while Amazon ECS can be used for processing heavier analytics tasks. This combination allows for cost-effective scaling based on demand.\n\nFor data storage, Amazon DynamoDB is selected due to its ability to handle massive amounts of data with low-latency responses, which is crucial for an analytics dashboard. It can seamlessly scale to accommodate spikes in traffic without manual intervention. Amazon Kinesis is included to handle real-time data streaming, enabling the dashboard to reflect analytics in near real-time. The monitoring layer employs Amazon CloudWatch for tracking performance and health metrics, ensuring reliability and quick response to any issues."
