    "reasoning": "For this architecture, AWS IoT Core is chosen as the edge service to securely connect and manage the IoT devices, ensuring reliable communication. The use of Amazon Kinesis allows for real-time processing of incoming sensor data streams, which is essential for handling high throughput from 100,000 devices. AWS Lambda is utilized for event-driven processing of data, while Amazon EC2 instances can be employed for more extensive processing tasks that require custom computation. The database layer includes Amazon DynamoDB for low-latency access to time-series data and Amazon RDS for relational data needs, facilitating efficient data storage and retrieval.\n\nReliability is prioritized by leveraging managed services such as AWS Lambda and Amazon Kinesis, which automatically scale to handle varying loads. This architecture also incorporates Amazon CloudWatch for monitoring system performance and health, enabling proactive management of resources. In terms of cost, the combination of serverless and on-demand services offers flexibility, allowing the architecture to adapt to fluctuating workloads without incurring unnecessary expenses."
