The architecture also incorporates Amazon ECS (Fargate) for container orchestration, allowing the client to run applications without managing the underlying infrastructure. This serverless approach to compute resources enables automatic scaling based on demand, which is essential for handling fluctuating traffic patterns. The use of an Application Load Balancer (ALB) allows for efficient routing of requests to the appropriate services, while Amazon CloudFront serves as a global content delivery network (CDN) to cache responses at the edge, further enhancing performance and reducing latency for end-users."
