    "reasoning": "In this architecture, Amazon CloudFront serves as a CDN to deliver low-latency access to the API Gateway, which handles incoming requests from the IoT devices. The API Gateway is integrated with AWS Lambda for serverless compute needs, ensuring no server management overhead and enabling auto-scaling to handle bursts of data from the 100k devices. Amazon ECS is utilized for containerized applications that require more control over the deployment, providing flexibility for custom processing logic.\n\nFor data storage, Amazon DynamoDB is chosen for its high availability and scalability, which is crucial for handling the massive influx of sensor data. The data is first streamed into Amazon Kinesis, allowing real-time processing and analytics, while Amazon SNS is used for notifications and alerts to ensure timely responses to critical events. This architecture allows for zero-downtime deployments by using blue/green deployment strategies in ECS and versioning in Lambda.\n\nThe use of these services supports a cost-effective solution, as the pay-as-you-go model for AWS services minimizes upfront investment, while ensuring that the architecture can scale dynamically with the number of IoT devices without service interruptions.",
