      "when_to_switch": "If the application evolves to require more horizontal scalability and handles mostly unstructured data, Amazon DynamoDB could be a better fit."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Amazon ECS vs Amazon EKS",
      "chose": "Amazon ECS",
      "reason": "Amazon ECS simplifies container orchestration and is easier to set up and manage for teams already familiar with AWS services, making it a better choice for a migration project.",
      "when_to_switch": "If the organization grows and requires more complex container management or Kubernetes-specific features, switching to Amazon EKS might be beneficial."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Application Load Balancer vs Network Load Balancer",
      "chose": "Application Load Balancer",
      "reason": "Application Load Balancer provides advanced routing capabilities and is better suited for HTTP/HTTPS traffic, which aligns with our web application needs.",
      "when_to_switch": "If there is a need for ultra-low latency TCP connections or if the application becomes heavily reliant on non-HTTP protocols, a Network Load Balancer may be more appropriate."
