    "reasoning": "To achieve high throughput, AWS Lambda is chosen for its ability to scale automatically with the number of incoming requests, handling spikes in traffic without pre-provisioning. Amazon ECS is utilized for processing complex business logic that requires longer execution times or specific dependencies. The combination of these compute services ensures that the architecture can handle the required transaction throughput while maintaining low latency.\n\nFor data storage, Amazon DynamoDB is selected for its ability to provide single-digit millisecond responses at scale, making it ideal for real-time applications. Additionally, Amazon ElastiCache is employed to cache frequently accessed data, reducing the load on DynamoDB and improving overall performance. The messaging layer leverages Amazon Kinesis for real-time data streaming, allowing the system to process and analyze transactions in real-time.\n\nThe use of Amazon API Gateway and Application Load Balancer enables efficient routing of requests and handling of incoming traffic, while Amazon CloudFront serves as a CDN that can speed up global access to the application, ensuring users experience minimal latency.",
