        "Amazon DynamoDB"
      ],
      "messaging": [
        "Amazon Kinesis"
      ],
      "monitoring": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch"
      ]
    },
    "reasoning": "The architecture leverages Amazon CloudFront to distribute traffic globally, reducing latency for users accessing the leaderboard. Using Amazon API Gateway allows for seamless management of API endpoints and helps in scaling the requests efficiently. AWS Lambda and Amazon ECS are used for compute, where Lambda can handle bursts of requests while ECS can manage longer-running processes, ensuring that the architecture can adapt to varying workloads. \n\nFor the database layer, Amazon DynamoDB is chosen for its ability to handle high write and read throughput, which is essential for real-time updates to the leaderboard. Its managed nature allows for automatic scaling and high availability, reducing operational overhead. Amazon Kinesis is integrated for real-time data streaming, enabling the processing of player scores and events in real-time. Overall, this architecture prioritizes scalability and reliability, catering to the high throughput demands of the game.",
    "trade_offs": [
      {
        "decision": "AWS Lambda vs Amazon ECS",
        "chose": "AWS Lambda",
        "reason": "Lambda is better for handling sudden bursts of requests due to its serverless nature and automatic scaling.",
        "when_to_switch": "If workloads become consistently high and predictable, moving to Amazon ECS may provide better cost efficiency and control."
      },
      {
        "decision": "Amazon DynamoDB vs Amazon RDS",
        "chose": "Amazon DynamoDB",
        "reason": "DynamoDB's ability to handle high-velocity data and automatic scaling makes it ideal for the leaderboard use case.",
        "when_to_switch": "If complex querying becomes necessary, Amazon RDS could be considered for SQL capabilities."
      },
      {
        "decision": "Amazon API Gateway vs Elastic Load Balancing",
        "chose": "Amazon API Gateway",
        "reason": "API Gateway simplifies the process of managing APIs and provides built-in throttling, authorization, and monitoring.",
        "when_to_switch": "For non-API traffic or if using a microservices architecture that requires more granular traffic management, Elastic Load Balancing would be better."
      }
    ],
    "cost": {
      "monthly_breakdown": [
        {
          "service": "Amazon CloudFront",
          "monthly_usd": 50.0,
          "unit": "data transfer and requests"
        },
        {
          "service": "Amazon API Gateway",
          "monthly_usd": 100.0,
          "unit": "API calls"
        },
        {
          "service": "AWS Lambda",
          "monthly_usd": 30.0,
          "unit": "invocations"
        },
        {
          "service": "Amazon ECS",
          "monthly_usd": 40.0,
          "unit": "compute"
        },
        {
          "service": "Amazon DynamoDB",
          "monthly_usd": 150.0,
          "unit": "read and write capacity"
        },
        {
          "service": "Amazon Kinesis",
          "monthly_usd": 50.0,
          "unit": "shard usage"
        },
        {
          "service": "Amazon CloudWatch",
          "monthly_usd": 10.0,
          "unit": "monitoring"
        }
      ],
      "total_monthly_usd": 430.0,
      "spike_estimate_usd": 600.0,
      "optimization": "Consider using reserved capacity for Amazon DynamoDB to reduce costs based on predictable traffic patterns."
    },
    "terraform": "resource \"aws_vpc\" \"main\" {  cidr_block = \"10.0.0.0/16\"  enable_dns_support = true  enable_dns_hostnames = true  tags = {    Name = \"main-vpc\"  }}\n\nresource \"aws_subnet\" \"public\" {  vpc_id     = aws_vpc.main.id  cidr_block = \"10.0.1.0/24\"  availability_zone = \"us-east-1a\"  map_public_ip_on_launch = true  tags = {    Name = \"public-subnet\"  }}\n\nresource \"aws_security_group\" \"api_sg\" {  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id  ingress {    from_port   = 80    to_port     = 80    protocol    = \"tcp\"    cidr_blocks = [\"0.0.0.0/0\"]  }  egress {    from_port   = 0    to_port     = 0    protocol    = \"-1\"    cidr_blocks = [\"0.0.0.0/0\"]  }  tags = {    Name = \"api-sg\"  }}\n\nresource \"aws_api_gateway_rest_api\" \"api\" {  name        = \"leaderboard-api\"  description = \"API for leaderboard\"}\n\nresource \"aws_lambda_function\" \"leaderboard_function\" {  function_name = \"leaderboardUpdater\"  handler = \"index.handler\"  runtime = \"nodejs14.x\"  role = aws_iam_role.lambda_exec.arn  }\n\nresource \"aws_dynamodb_table\" \"leaderboard_table\" {  name           = \"leaderboard\"  billing_mode   = \"PAY_PER_REQUEST\"  attribute {    name = \"playerId\"    type = \"S\"  }  key_schema {    hash_key = \"playerId\"  }}\n\nresource \"aws_kinesis_stream\" \"leaderboard_stream\" {  name        = \"leaderboardStream\"  shard_count = 1}\n\nresource \"aws_cloudwatch_log_group\" \"log_group\" {  name = \"/aws/lambda/leaderboardUpdater\"  retention_in_days = 14}",
    "diagram": "graph TD\n    User([User])\n    User -->|API Call| APIGateway([Amazon API Gateway])\n    APIGateway -->|Trigger| Lambda([AWS Lambda])\n    Lambda -->|Update| DynamoDB([Amazon DynamoDB])\n    Lambda -->|Stream| Kinesis([Amazon Kinesis])\n    Kinesis -->|Stream Data| Analytics[Analytics Service]\n    subgraph CDN\n    CloudFront([Amazon CloudFront])\n    end\n    CloudFront -->|Content Delivery| User"
  }
}

