    "reasoning": "To ensure GDPR compliance while processing real-time sensor data from a large number of IoT devices, Amazon Kinesis is chosen for its ability to handle high-throughput data streams reliably. AWS Lambda is used to process incoming data in real-time, providing a serverless architecture that scales automatically as data volume fluctuates. The combination of Amazon DynamoDB for storing structured data and Amazon RDS for relational data ensures both scalability and flexibility in managing data while adhering to GDPR regulations.\n\nAmazon CloudFront is utilized as a CDN to deliver content with low latency and high transfer speeds, ensuring user data is handled efficiently. The architecture leverages Amazon API Gateway to provide a secure entry point for IoT devices to send data, while AWS Global Accelerator optimizes the path to the API. This design not only maintains data integrity and availability but also minimizes costs due to the pay-as-you-go model of serverless services."
