    "reasoning": "Using Amazon S3 for storage allows for scalable and cost-effective storage of user-uploaded videos. AWS Lambda can be used for serverless processing of events such as uploads, while Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS) can handle the heavy lifting of transcoding. The combination of AWS Lambda and ECS provides a flexible architecture that can scale based on demand, allowing for efficient processing of multiple video files simultaneously.\n\nAmazon CloudFront will serve as the Content Delivery Network (CDN) to deliver the transcoded videos efficiently to end-users, ensuring low latencies. Amazon SNS can be used to notify users of the completion of their transcoding jobs, while SQS can queue the transcoding tasks to handle spikes in upload volumes, ensuring reliability and robustness in the processing pipeline. Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch will allow for visibility into the system's performance and operational health."
