      ]
    },
    "reasoning": "For the compute layer, AWS Lambda is chosen for its ability to automatically scale in response to incoming requests, which is essential for handling spikes in document uploads. Additionally, Amazon ECS can be utilized for more complex processing tasks that require container orchestration, making the solution flexible and cost-effective. The use of Amazon S3 for storage allows for durable and scalable storage of the PDFs, while Amazon DynamoDB provides a fast NoSQL database for metadata management, enabling quick lookups of processed documents.\n\nIn the messaging layer, Amazon SQS is employed to decouple the PDF upload process from the processing workflows, ensuring that the system remains responsive even during high loads. Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch allows for real-time insights into system performance and can trigger alarms based on specific metrics, ensuring reliability. The architecture is designed to minimize costs by utilizing serverless technologies where applicable, while still maintaining the capability to scale as needed."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
