    "reasoning": "The use of Amazon CloudFront provides a reliable Content Delivery Network (CDN) to serve static assets and enhance performance for users globally. Amazon API Gateway allows for efficient management of RESTful APIs, and AWS Global Accelerator improves the availability and performance of the application. For compute, AWS Lambda is chosen for its scalability and cost-effectiveness, as it can handle varying loads without requiring server management. Additionally, Amazon ECS is used for running containerized services, allowing for a flexible architecture that can scale based on demand.\n\nFor the database layer, Amazon DynamoDB is selected due to its ability to handle high throughput and its managed nature, which eliminates the operational overhead. Amazon ElastiCache is employed to improve performance by caching frequently accessed data. Amazon Kinesis is used to manage the ingestion of up to 10 million messages per day, providing real-time data processing capabilities. Monitoring services like Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray ensure that performance metrics are tracked and any issues can be diagnosed promptly."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
    {
