    "reasoning": "The architecture leverages Amazon CloudFront as a Content Delivery Network (CDN) to cache static content and reduce latency for users globally. AWS WAF is integrated with CloudFront to provide a web application firewall that protects against common web exploits, while also offering bot protection features to mitigate automated attacks. The Elastic Load Balancer (ELB) distributes incoming traffic across multiple EC2 instances, ensuring high availability and reliability. For compute, AWS Lambda can be used for serverless functions, while EC2 instances can be set up in an Auto Scaling group to handle variable traffic loads efficiently.

For data storage, Amazon RDS is chosen for structured data needs, providing managed relational database services, while DynamoDB serves as a scalable NoSQL solution for unstructured data. This combination allows for flexibility in data management. Amazon SQS is included for messaging between microservices, ensuring decoupled architecture. Monitoring is handled through Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray, providing insights into application performance and operational health, which is crucial for maintaining a seamless user experience in an e-commerce environment."
