    "reasoning": "Using Amazon CloudFront at the edge layer helps reduce latency by caching responses and serving them closer to the users. AWS Global Accelerator ensures that traffic is routed through the optimal path across AWS regions, improving reliability and performance. For compute, AWS Lambda is chosen for its ability to automatically scale in response to incoming requests, while Amazon ECS manages containerized applications that can handle heavy loads. This combination ensures that the architecture can handle the high throughput of 50,000 predictions per second efficiently.\n\nAmazon DynamoDB is selected as the database due to its ability to scale horizontally and handle high request rates with low latency. It's a fully managed NoSQL database that fits well with the needs of machine learning model serving. Integrating Amazon SQS allows for decoupling of components, enabling asynchronous processing which is crucial for high-load scenarios. Additionally, Amazon CloudWatch provides monitoring capabilities to track performance metrics and ensure smooth operation across the infrastructure."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
