    "reasoning": "Using Amazon CloudFront as a CDN ensures low latency and improved performance for users accessing the insurance portal globally. The AWS Application Load Balancer and Amazon API Gateway provide a robust networking layer that facilitates routing and management of API calls while enabling features like rate limiting and caching. For compute, AWS Lambda allows for serverless execution of event-driven functions, while Amazon ECS is used for containerized applications that can scale based on demand. This combination supports high availability and low latency processing of 1,000 events per minute.\n\nFor the database layer, Amazon Aurora is chosen for its high performance and scalability, allowing for automatic scaling based on traffic patterns and providing read replicas for load distribution. Amazon ElastiCache can be utilized to cache frequently accessed data, reducing the load on the database and improving response times. The messaging layer with Amazon SQS facilitates decoupling of services, ensuring that messages are reliably queued and processed even during traffic spikes. Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray provides insights into system performance, enabling proactive adjustments and ensuring zero downtime through effective health checks and alerting."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
