      "messaging": [
        "Amazon Kinesis"
      ],
      "monitoring": [
        "Amazon CloudWatch"
      ]
    },
    "reasoning": "Using Amazon CloudFront will help deliver static content quickly to users around the globe, providing low latency. The combination of Amazon API Gateway and an Application Load Balancer allows for efficient routing and management of incoming requests to Lambda functions and ECS services, ensuring high availability and fault tolerance. AWS Lambda is ideal for handling unpredictable workloads and can scale up automatically to accommodate spikes in user activity without the need for provisioning servers, which reduces operational overhead.\n\nAmazon DynamoDB is a fully managed NoSQL database that can handle large volumes of read and write requests, making it suitable for a real-time leaderboard that needs to support high throughput. It offers built-in scalability and durability, ensuring that player scores are always available and consistent. For real-time data processing, Amazon Kinesis is chosen to capture and process streaming data, allowing for immediate updates to the leaderboard as player scores change. This architecture is designed to be cost-effective while meeting the performance requirements of a large user base."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
    {
      "decision": "AWS Lambda vs Amazon ECS",
      "chose": "AWS Lambda",
      "reason": "AWS Lambda is better for sporadic workloads and provides automatic scaling without server management.",
      "when_to_switch": "If the application requires long-running processes or a need for custom runtimes, Amazon ECS may be a better fit."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Amazon DynamoDB vs Amazon RDS",
      "chose": "Amazon DynamoDB",
      "reason": "DynamoDB is optimized for high-speed reads and writes, making it ideal for real-time leaderboard updates.",
      "when_to_switch": "If complex queries and transactions become necessary, or if relational data modeling is required, Amazon RDS would be more appropriate."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Amazon API Gateway vs Application Load Balancer",
      "chose": "Amazon API Gateway",
      "reason": "API Gateway simplifies the process of creating, deploying, and managing APIs, providing built-in security and throttling.",
      "when_to_switch": "If there is a need for WebSocket support or advanced routing capabilities, an Application Load Balancer might be preferred."
    }
  ],
  "cost": {
