    "reasoning": "For this real-time bidding platform, using Amazon CloudFront as a CDN offers low latency and high availability to users globally. The combination of Amazon API Gateway and Application Load Balancer provides a managed way to route traffic efficiently while scaling automatically with demand. AWS Lambda is chosen for its serverless capabilities, allowing for on-demand execution of bidding functions without provisioning servers, leading to cost savings during low traffic periods. Amazon ECS is used for containerized applications that require consistent performance and quick scaling during peak times.\n\nIn terms of data storage, Amazon DynamoDB is an excellent choice due to its low-latency access and ability to handle high request rates, which is crucial for a bidding platform. Additionally, Amazon ElastiCache is used to cache frequently accessed data to improve response times further. For real-time data streaming and processing, Amazon Kinesis provides the capabilities required to handle a large volume of bids and user interactions. Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray ensures performance tracking and debugging capabilities, essential for maintaining service reliability and user experience.",
