    },
    "reasoning": "Using Amazon CloudFront as a CDN helps reduce latency and provides caching capabilities for static assets, improving response times for users. The AWS Application Load Balancer (ALB) efficiently distributes incoming API calls to multiple AWS Lambda functions and ECS tasks, ensuring high availability and scalability. AWS Lambda allows for serverless compute, which automatically scales with request volume, making it cost-effective for fluctuating workloads. For processing complex queries and transactions, Amazon RDS provides a reliable relational database solution, while Amazon DynamoDB offers high throughput and low latency for NoSQL data storage, essential for user and ride data.\n\nTo ensure messaging between microservices is decoupled and reliable, Amazon SQS is employed for asynchronous communication. This architecture balances performance, reliability, and cost, enabling the ride-sharing platform to handle a high volume of requests while minimizing operational overhead. The monitoring capabilities of Amazon CloudWatch provide insights into application performance and user activity, allowing for proactive scaling and issue resolution."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
