    "reasoning": "Using Amazon CloudFront as the CDN helps to accelerate content delivery and improve response times for users accessing the legal documents. The Elastic Load Balancing in conjunction with Amazon API Gateway provides a robust way to manage incoming requests efficiently, ensuring high availability and automatic scaling to handle varying loads. AWS Lambda is chosen for compute needs as it allows for a serverless architecture that scales automatically based on the number of transactions, which is ideal for the varying workloads associated with legal documents. Amazon ECS can be utilized for containerized applications that require consistent performance and scaling capabilities.\n\nFor the database layer, Amazon DynamoDB is selected due to its ability to handle high transaction loads with low latency, which is crucial for a document system that may see bursts of activity. Its NoSQL structure is well-suited for the flexible data models typically involved in legal documentation. The messaging layer uses Amazon SQS to ensure reliable message queuing between services, which adds resilience to the architecture by decoupling components. Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch allows for real-time insights into system performance, which is critical for maintaining service levels in a legal context.",
