For networking, using an Elastic Load Balancer (ELB) in conjunction with Amazon Route 53 allows for efficient traffic distribution and DNS management. This combination ensures that the application can handle varying loads and provides a robust failover mechanism. The choice of databases like Amazon RDS and DynamoDB offers flexibility in data storage, where RDS can be used for relational data and DynamoDB for NoSQL workloads, catering to different application needs. Overall, this architecture is designed to be cost-effective while maintaining high performance and reliability."
