For database management, Amazon RDS is selected for its managed PostgreSQL service, which integrates natively with AWS Secrets Manager for automated credential rotation. This ensures that database credentials remain secure and up-to-date without manual intervention. ElastiCache is used for caching frequently accessed data, improving application performance and reducing database load. The use of Amazon SQS allows for decoupling components of the architecture, ensuring that the application can handle spikes in traffic without downtime, as messages can be processed asynchronously. Overall, this architecture is designed to be robust, scalable, and cost-efficient, adhering to best practices for secrets management and application deployment."
