    "reasoning": "Using Amazon CloudFront as a CDN will help deliver podcast content quickly to users, reducing latency. The Application Load Balancer will distribute incoming traffic efficiently to services running on Amazon ECS and AWS Lambda. The compute layer leverages AWS Lambda for serverless execution of lightweight tasks and Amazon ECS for more resource-intensive processes, ensuring scalability as traffic varies. The architecture is designed for zero-downtime deployments using blue/green or canary strategies in ECS, enabling smooth transitions between application versions.\n\nOn the database side, Amazon DynamoDB is chosen for its high read and write throughput, which is essential for handling the 5M records per day efficiently. Amazon RDS will be used for relational data needs, providing the required ACID properties. The combination of DynamoDB's scalability and RDS's relational capabilities allows for a flexible data layer. Amazon SQS will be utilized for decoupling components and ensuring reliable message delivery, which is crucial for maintaining system responsiveness during high loads. Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray will ensure observability and help in troubleshooting issues promptly, enhancing overall reliability.",
