    "reasoning": "For low latency and high scalability, Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) is chosen to orchestrate containerized applications that can dynamically scale based on incoming prediction requests. Using EKS allows for efficient resource management and rapid deployment of machine learning models. AWS Lambda can be leveraged for infrequent, bursty prediction requests, providing a serverless option that scales automatically. Amazon CloudFront acts as a Content Delivery Network (CDN) to cache responses closer to users, further reducing latency.\n\nAmazon DynamoDB is selected as the database for its ability to handle high-throughput workloads with low-latency data access, which is critical when serving predictions quickly. Its managed nature ensures reliability and scalability without the need for manual intervention. Amazon CloudWatch provides monitoring to keep track of application performance and resource utilization, enabling proactive scaling decisions and ensuring that the architecture remains performant under load."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
    {
      "decision": "Amazon EKS vs AWS Fargate",
