    "reasoning": "Using Amazon CloudFront as a CDN will reduce latency by caching content closer to users, enhancing performance for the dashboard. The Elastic Load Balancing and Amazon API Gateway will effectively distribute incoming traffic across multiple AWS Lambda functions and Amazon ECS containers, ensuring that the architecture can scale horizontally to meet the demand of handling 20,000 events per minute. AWS Lambda provides a serverless compute option that automatically scales with the load while keeping costs low for variable workloads.\n\nFor data storage, Amazon Aurora is chosen for relational data due to its high availability and read scalability, while Amazon DynamoDB serves as a NoSQL solution for handling large volumes of events with low latency. Amazon Kinesis is included to manage real-time data streams, which is essential for processing events as they come in. This combination allows the architecture to maintain reliability under heavy load while optimizing costs by using serverless components and managed services that reduce operational overhead.",
