    "reasoning": "AWS Lambda is chosen for compute due to its serverless nature, which reduces operational overhead and allows the client to focus on application logic instead of managing servers. It scales automatically to handle varying loads, making it ideal for the expected transaction volume of 1k per day. Amazon DynamoDB is selected as the database for its fully managed NoSQL capabilities, enabling fast and predictable performance with seamless scaling. This combination ensures high availability and low latency for the mobile banking app without the complexities of managing infrastructure.\n\nUsing Amazon API Gateway simplifies routing and handling of HTTP requests, providing built-in features such as throttling and authorization, which are crucial for a banking application. Amazon CloudFront serves as a CDN to enhance content delivery speed and reduce latency for end-users. Additionally, Amazon SNS can be utilized for notifications, such as transaction alerts, which enhances user engagement. Overall, this architecture prioritizes simplicity, allowing for easy management and scalability as traffic increases."
