For the database layer, Amazon RDS is selected to run SAP HANA, providing managed database services with automated backups and scaling capabilities. Amazon DynamoDB is included for any NoSQL requirements, allowing for high throughput and low latency access to data. Messaging services like Amazon SQS and SNS are integrated to facilitate decoupled communication between microservices, enhancing the system's reliability and scalability. Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray ensures observability and performance tracking across the hybrid architecture."
