    "reasoning": "To handle 1 million PDFs per day, we leverage Amazon S3 for scalable storage of the documents, ensuring that data is stored securely and cost-effectively. AWS Lambda manages the initial processing of the PDFs in a serverless manner, allowing for automatic scaling as the workload fluctuates. Amazon ECS is used for more complex processing tasks that require container orchestration, ensuring high availability and reliability.\n\nThe architecture incorporates Amazon CloudFront as a CDN to distribute content globally with low latency, which is essential for user access. The AWS Application Load Balancer directs incoming traffic to the appropriate compute resources, enhancing performance and reliability. For data management, Amazon RDS provides structured querying capabilities, while Amazon DynamoDB offers low-latency access for metadata, ensuring compliance with GDPR by enabling easy data retrieval and management. Messaging through Amazon SQS ensures that the pipeline remains decoupled, allowing for robust error handling and processing flow control.",
