    "reasoning": "To achieve high availability and low latency for 4K video content delivery, Amazon CloudFront is chosen as the CDN service. It caches the content at edge locations around the world, ensuring that users have quick access to the video streams. AWS Global Accelerator enhances the performance of the application by directing user traffic to optimal endpoints, minimizing latency. For compute, AWS Lambda is selected to handle on-demand processing tasks, while Amazon EC2 instances can be utilized for more consistent workloads that require more control and configuration, such as encoding or transcoding video content.\n\nUsing Amazon S3 as the storage layer is ideal for storing and serving large video files. It provides durability, scalability, and cost-effectiveness. The architecture leverages Amazon CloudWatch for monitoring metrics and logs, allowing proactive management of resources and ensuring application health. This setup ensures that the infrastructure can scale according to demand, providing a seamless experience for users accessing 4K content."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
    {
      "decision": "AWS Lambda vs Amazon EC2",
