      "reason": "AWS Lambda is suitable for on-demand processing without the need to manage servers, making it cost-effective for sporadic workloads.",
      "when_to_switch": "If processing demands become consistent and require more control over the environment, switching to Amazon EC2 would be beneficial."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Amazon S3 vs Amazon EFS",
      "chose": "Amazon S3",
      "reason": "Amazon S3 provides better performance for serving large files and is more cost-effective for high-volume storage of video content.",
      "when_to_switch": "If there is a need for low-latency file access with shared file systems, Amazon EFS would be more appropriate."
