    "reasoning": "To support 500 engineering teams effectively, the architecture leverages Amazon CloudFront for content delivery, ensuring low latency for global users. The use of AWS Lambda enables scalable and cost-efficient execution of CI/CD pipelines without the need to manage server infrastructure. Amazon ECS allows for container orchestration, providing an efficient way to deploy applications in a microservices architecture, ensuring that resources are utilized effectively. On the database side, Amazon RDS provides a relational database solution for storing application metadata, while Amazon DynamoDB offers a NoSQL solution for high-throughput requirements, making it suitable for handling varying workloads.\n\nThe AWS Application Load Balancer distributes incoming traffic evenly across multiple instances, enhancing reliability and availability. Amazon API Gateway serves as a front door for the APIs, allowing for easy management and monitoring of API calls. This architecture supports horizontal scaling, helping to manage the high demand from multiple teams while maintaining cost efficiency. With a combination of managed services, the solution provides a robust and reliable environment for CI/CD operations, allowing teams to focus on development rather than infrastructure management."
