    "reasoning": "The use of Amazon CloudFront ensures low-latency access to the application through edge locations, optimizing the user experience. AWS Global Accelerator provides a single entry point while directing traffic to the closest region, enhancing the performance of the multi-region architecture. For compute, AWS Lambda is chosen for its ability to scale automatically with the transaction load, while Amazon ECS manages containerized applications effectively. This combination allows for high availability and responsiveness during traffic spikes.\n\nAmazon DynamoDB offers a fully managed NoSQL database solution that can handle high throughput with low latency, making it suitable for real-time processing of fraud detection data. Additionally, Amazon ElastiCache is employed to store frequently accessed data in-memory, further enhancing response times. For messaging, Amazon Kinesis enables real-time data streaming, allowing the system to process and analyze incoming transaction data as it arrives. Monitoring is handled by Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray for performance insights and operational health, ensuring reliability.",
