    "reasoning": "To handle 10 million concurrent users, Amazon CloudFront is utilized as a CDN to cache static assets and reduce latency. The Application Load Balancer will distribute incoming traffic efficiently across multiple Amazon ECS containers, ensuring high availability and scalability. AWS Lambda is integrated for handling serverless computing tasks, allowing for dynamic scaling based on user demand without incurring costs during low-traffic periods.\n\nFor the database layer, Amazon RDS is chosen for relational data management with high availability, while Amazon DynamoDB provides a NoSQL solution for handling large volumes of unstructured data. This combination ensures both performance and flexibility. Amazon SQS is included for decoupling services and managing communication between components, which enhances reliability and scalability. Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch will provide insights into performance and trigger scaling actions as needed.",
