        "Amazon CloudWatch"
      ]
    },
    "reasoning": "The use of Amazon CloudFront as a CDN ensures low-latency delivery of video content to end-users, improving the overall user experience. An Elastic Load Balancer and Amazon API Gateway manage incoming requests seamlessly, allowing for a scalable and reliable architecture that can handle varying loads. For compute, AWS Lambda is utilized for lightweight tasks, such as triggering the transcoding process, while Amazon ECS can handle more complex transcoding workloads, allowing developers to choose the right level of abstraction for their needs.\n\nAmazon S3 serves as a durable and scalable storage solution for user-uploaded videos and transcoded outputs. Amazon DynamoDB provides a fast and flexible NoSQL database solution to manage metadata related to the videos, such as upload status or user information. Using Amazon SQS allows for asynchronous processing of transcoding jobs, ensuring that the system can scale effectively without overwhelming any single component. This combination of services provides a robust foundation for a developer-friendly experience while maintaining flexibility and reliability across the architecture."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
    {
      "decision": "AWS Lambda vs Amazon ECS for compute",
      "chose": "AWS Lambda",
      "reason": "AWS Lambda is serverless and allows for quick deployments and easy scaling for lightweight tasks, which fits well with a developer-focused approach.",
      "when_to_switch": "If the transcoding tasks become too resource-intensive or exceed Lambda's execution time limit, then switching to Amazon ECS would be more appropriate."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Amazon DynamoDB vs Amazon RDS for database",
      "chose": "Amazon DynamoDB",
      "reason": "Amazon DynamoDB provides automatic scaling and low-latency access without the need for complex management, making it easier for developers to focus on application logic.",
      "when_to_switch": "If there is a requirement for complex querying or transactions, then Amazon RDS would be a better fit."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Elastic Load Balancer vs Amazon API Gateway for networking",
      "chose": "Amazon API Gateway",
      "reason": "Amazon API Gateway provides built-in support for REST APIs, enabling rapid development and easier integration with Lambda functions, which is beneficial for developers.",
      "when_to_switch": "If the system needs to handle traditional web traffic or requires advanced load balancing capabilities, then an Elastic Load Balancer would be more suitable."
    }
  ],
