    {
      "decision": "Amazon RDS vs Amazon DynamoDB",
      "chose": "Amazon RDS",
      "reason": "RDS is better suited for structured data and complex queries related to historical alert data and metrics, which is crucial for SLO/SLA analysis.",
      "when_to_switch": "If the application requires high-speed access to key-value pairs or needs to scale horizontally for massive workloads, DynamoDB would be more appropriate."
