    "reasoning": "Using Amazon ECS with AWS Fargate allows for a serverless approach to run containers, enabling seamless scaling based on demand. This is crucial for a video transcoding pipeline that may experience spikes in user uploads. The Application Load Balancer will distribute incoming requests to the ECS services efficiently, ensuring high availability and reliability. By utilizing Amazon CloudFront, we can cache and deliver video content to end-users globally while optimizing load times, which enhances user experience.\n\nFor storage, Amazon S3 is ideal for storing user-uploaded videos due to its durability and scalability, as it can handle a vast amount of data without manual intervention. Amazon DynamoDB is chosen for metadata storage due to its low-latency performance and ability to scale automatically with traffic. Additionally, Amazon SQS will help decouple the components of the pipeline, allowing for smooth message passing between the uploader, transcoding service, and storage, thereby improving the overall resilience of the architecture."
