The architecture leverages Amazon S3 for object storage, which is cost-effective and provides durability for large datasets. Amazon CloudFront can be used as a CDN to cache frequently accessed data closer to the compute resources, improving performance. The networking layer, built on Amazon VPC and AWS Transit Gateway, ensures secure and efficient communication between various components of the architecture. Monitoring and observability are handled by Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray, which provide insights into performance and help identify bottlenecks in the HPC workloads."
