    "cost considerations are also favorable, as S3 provides a pay-as-you-go model, allowing the client to scale storage and replication needs without upfront costs.": "The chosen architecture leverages AWS's global infrastructure to ensure high availability and low latency for users across different regions. By utilizing Amazon Route 53 for DNS routing, the architecture can direct users to the nearest S3 bucket, further enhancing performance."
