    "reasoning": "To handle 10M requests per second, we are leveraging AWS Lambda for its serverless capabilities, allowing for automatic scaling based on incoming requests. This reduces the need for upfront capacity planning and provides cost efficiency, as you only pay for the compute time consumed. Amazon ECS is used for containerized processing of podcast data, providing flexibility to manage workloads effectively. The combination of AWS Lambda and Amazon ECS ensures that we can scale both stateless and stateful components as needed.\n\nFor data storage, Amazon DynamoDB is chosen for its high throughput and low-latency performance, which is crucial for handling such a high number of requests. It also supports automatic scaling, which aligns with our event-driven approach. Amazon SQS will be used to decouple the components of our architecture, allowing for reliable message queuing which is essential for event-driven systems. Finally, integrating Amazon CloudWatch enables effective monitoring of the entire system, ensuring we can maintain performance and reliability under heavy load."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
    {
