    "reasoning": "The architecture leverages Amazon CloudFront to provide low-latency access to the application globally, improving user experience by caching static and dynamic content. The Application Load Balancer and Amazon API Gateway enable efficient routing of incoming requests, ensuring high availability and scalability as user demand fluctuates. AWS Lambda facilitates a serverless compute model, allowing for automatic scaling based on the number of events processed, which is critical for handling the expected 1 million events per minute without the overhead of managing server instances.\n\nFor data storage, Amazon Aurora is used for relational data that requires ACID compliance, while Amazon DynamoDB serves high-throughput NoSQL needs, ensuring rapid access to user data. The use of Amazon Kinesis allows for real-time data processing, enabling the application to handle streaming events efficiently. Monitoring tools like Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray provide insights into application performance and help diagnose issues, ensuring reliability and performance optimization over time.",
    "trade_offs": [
      {
