    "reasoning": "For an e-commerce platform expecting 10 million concurrent users, scalability and reliability are paramount. Amazon CloudFront serves as a CDN to cache static content and reduce latency for users worldwide. Elastic Load Balancing ensures that incoming traffic is distributed across multiple EC2 instances and ECS containers, providing fault tolerance and minimizing downtime. AWS Lambda can handle asynchronous workloads, such as order processing, allowing for elastic scaling without provisioning servers.\n\nThe database layer utilizes Amazon RDS for relational data with Multi-AZ deployments for high availability, while Amazon DynamoDB handles high-velocity transactions with its serverless nature and seamless scaling capabilities. ElastiCache is employed to cache frequently accessed data, thus reducing database load and improving response times. Messaging services like SQS and SNS facilitate communication between microservices, ensuring decoupling and reliability in processing events. Monitoring with CloudWatch and X-Ray allows for real-time insights and troubleshooting, maintaining operational reliability.",
