    "reasoning": "AWS Lambda provides a scalable compute solution that automatically adjusts to traffic demands, allowing the application to handle varying workloads without the need for manual intervention. By using Amazon DynamoDB, the architecture can leverage its multi-tenant capabilities, ensuring data isolation through partition keys based on customer IDs. This approach minimizes management overhead and maximizes reliability, as AWS services are designed to be fault-tolerant and highly available. Furthermore, using Amazon API Gateway allows for easy management of API endpoints, enabling secure and scalable access to the backend services.\n\nThe use of Amazon CloudFront as a content delivery network ensures low latency and high transfer speeds for end-users, improving the overall user experience. Amazon SNS provides a simple way to decouple various parts of the system, facilitating notifications and messages between services without creating tight coupling. This architecture is cost-efficient as it utilizes a pay-as-you-go model, ensuring that the client only pays for the resources they use while providing the flexibility to scale as their customer base grows."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
    {
      "decision": "AWS Lambda vs Amazon ECS",
      "chose": "AWS Lambda",
      "reason": "AWS Lambda is more cost-effective for sporadic workloads and requires less management, making it ideal for a serverless architecture.",
      "when_to_switch": "If the application requires long-running processes or needs to maintain state across invocations, Amazon ECS may be more suitable."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Amazon DynamoDB vs Amazon RDS",
      "chose": "Amazon DynamoDB",
      "reason": "Amazon DynamoDB provides built-in support for multi-tenancy and scales automatically based on demand, which simplifies data isolation and management.",
      "when_to_switch": "If complex joins and relational queries are necessary, Amazon RDS would be a better fit."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Amazon API Gateway vs Application Load Balancer",
      "chose": "Amazon API Gateway",
      "reason": "Amazon API Gateway is designed specifically for API management, offering features like throttling and caching, which are beneficial for a serverless architecture.",
      "when_to_switch": "If you require advanced routing capabilities or need to serve a wide variety of protocols, an Application Load Balancer might be more appropriate."
    }
  ],
  "cost": {
