    "reasoning": "To handle the ingestion of 10TB of logs daily, we utilize Amazon S3 as the primary storage for the data lake, providing virtually unlimited storage capacity and durability. AWS Lambda is employed to process incoming log data in real-time, while Amazon Kinesis Data Streams allows for high-throughput log ingestion, enabling near real-time processing and analytics. Amazon EMR can be used for batch processing and transformation of the log data into structured formats, ideal for querying with Amazon Athena.\n\nFor networking, AWS Transit Gateway and Amazon API Gateway facilitate seamless integration and connectivity between services while maintaining security and performance. Monitoring is achieved through Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray to ensure the performance of the architecture and troubleshoot issues as they arise. This architecture provides scalability to accommodate increasing log volumes and reliability through the use of managed services that automatically handle failover and redundancy.",
