    "reasoning": "For a CI/CD platform serving a large number of engineering teams, scalability and reliability are crucial. AWS Lambda can be used for serverless functions that trigger on events such as code commits, allowing for flexible execution without managing servers. Amazon ECS provides container orchestration for microservices, making it easy to deploy applications at scale. AWS CodeBuild and CodeDeploy facilitate continuous integration and deployment, ensuring that code changes can be tested and deployed quickly. Using Amazon RDS for relational data requirements and Amazon DynamoDB for fast, scalable NoSQL data access helps support the varying needs of the teams.\n\nThe architecture also incorporates Amazon SNS for notifications and AWS Step Functions to coordinate complex workflows in the CI/CD process. This combination allows teams to easily manage the flow of code changes, providing a robust solution that can handle spikes in usage, such as during major releases or updates. Cost efficiency is achieved through the serverless components and managed services, reducing the overhead of maintaining infrastructure while providing high availability."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
