    },
    "reasoning": "AWS IoT Core is ideal for securely connecting and managing a large number of IoT devices, allowing for efficient data ingestion. AWS Lambda is a serverless compute option that scales automatically based on the volume of sensor data, ensuring cost efficiency as clients only pay for the compute time consumed. Amazon Kinesis provides real-time processing capabilities that allow for immediate insights from the sensor data, while Amazon DynamoDB offers a fully managed NoSQL database that scales seamlessly to accommodate the high throughput and low-latency requirements of the application.\n\nBy using serverless components such as AWS Lambda and fully managed services like DynamoDB, the architecture minimizes operational overhead and optimizes costs. This setup allows for a pay-as-you-go model, making it especially suitable for a scenario with fluctuating data loads from numerous IoT devices. Monitoring through Amazon CloudWatch ensures that the system can be observed and adjusted as needed, keeping operational costs in check and performance high."
  },
  "trade_offs": [
    {
      "decision": "AWS Lambda vs EC2",
      "chose": "AWS Lambda",
      "reason": "AWS Lambda is more cost-effective for variable workloads and scales automatically without the need to manage servers.",
      "when_to_switch": "If the workload becomes consistently high and predictable, EC2 might provide lower costs with reserved instances."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Amazon DynamoDB vs Amazon RDS",
      "chose": "Amazon DynamoDB",
      "reason": "Amazon DynamoDB is better suited for high-velocity data ingestion from IoT devices, offering low-latency access and automatic scaling.",
      "when_to_switch": "If complex queries and joins are required, Amazon RDS would be a better choice despite higher operational costs."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Amazon Kinesis vs Amazon SQS",
      "chose": "Amazon Kinesis",
      "reason": "Amazon Kinesis provides real-time processing capabilities which are essential for immediate insights from sensor data.",
      "when_to_switch": "If message processing can tolerate delays and does not require real-time analytics, Amazon SQS could be a more cost-effective solution."
    }
