    "reasoning": "The architecture utilizes Amazon CloudFront to cache and serve content at the edge, reducing latency for users. Elastic Load Balancing distributes incoming traffic across multiple instances of ECS, ensuring reliability and high availability. AWS Lambda is employed for event-driven processes, enabling the platform to handle spikes in bidding requests without the need for constant infrastructure provisioning.\n\nTo manage data, Amazon DynamoDB is chosen for its high performance and scalability, which is essential for storing real-time bidding data. Additionally, Amazon RDS provides a relational database option for transactional data and analytics. Amazon Kinesis is included to process incoming streams of bidding data in real-time, allowing for rapid decision-making during the bidding process. Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch ensures that system performance and health are continuously tracked, enabling quick responses to issues."
