    "reasoning": "The architecture leverages AWS Lambda for serverless compute, which allows for automatic scaling in response to incoming data processing requests, ensuring that the pipeline can handle spikes in workload without manual intervention. Amazon ECS and AWS Batch provide robust environments for running containerized tasks and batch jobs that process large datasets, optimizing resource usage and cost-effectiveness. The use of Amazon S3 as the primary data storage solution ensures durability and easy access to the terabytes of DNA sequences, while Amazon DynamoDB provides fast and scalable NoSQL database capabilities for metadata storage and quick lookups.\n\nFor networking, an Elastic Load Balancer (ELB) distributes incoming requests across the compute services, ensuring high availability and fault tolerance. The Amazon API Gateway allows for the secure exposure of RESTful APIs that clients can use to submit data for processing and retrieve results. Monitoring is crucial in ensuring the health and performance of the pipeline; thus, Amazon CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray are implemented to provide real-time insights and traceability into the workflow, enabling proactive management and optimization."
