    "reasoning": "In this architecture, CloudFront is chosen as the edge service to provide low-latency content delivery and caching for static assets, which is crucial for enhancing user experience. The Application Load Balancer (ALB) serves as the entry point for incoming traffic, distributing requests to EC2 instances running the web application. This setup allows for automatic scaling based on demand, ensuring high availability and reliability. The use of DynamoDB as a NoSQL database provides fast read/write capabilities for small data blobs, while RDS can be included if relational data storage is needed. This combination of services ensures that the architecture is both scalable and cost-effective, as you only pay for the resources you consume.",
