        "when_to_switch": "If the application requires dynamic content that needs to be processed on the server-side for every request, ALB may be more appropriate for routing traffic directly to compute resources."
      },
      {
        "decision": "DynamoDB vs RDS for data storage",
        "chose": "DynamoDB",
        "reason": "DynamoDB offers low-latency access for key-value pairs and scales automatically based on demand, making it ideal for workloads with unpredictable traffic patterns.",
        "when_to_switch": "If the application requires complex queries, transactions, or joins, RDS would be a better fit due to its relational capabilities."
